<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The "Habit grid" entry in the widget picker - M15.6b.

  ⚠⚠ targetCellWidth WAS 4 AND THE USER ASKED FOR SMALLER. On their phone (360dp wide, an 8-column
  launcher grid) four cells came out 176dp - just over half the screen - so two habits could not sit
  side by side with any spacing between them. Three cells is comfortably under half, which is what
  they asked for; minResizeWidth then lets them go smaller still by hand.

  minWidth/minHeight are the pre-31 fallback for targetCellWidth/Height and must stay in agreement
  with them.

  ⚠ resizeMode gained "vertical", and only because the drawing changed. It used to be horizontal
  only, on the sound argument that the grid's height is seven rows by definition - so vertical space
  had nothing to do. Since fitGrid() derives the DOT SIZE from the available height, a taller widget
  now draws a bigger grid, and vertical resizing does something the user can see.

  initialLayout is Glance's own loading layout - what shows between the widget being dropped and
  provideGlance returning.

  ⚠ No previewImage/previewLayout yet, so the picker shows a generic icon rather than a picture of
  the widget. Known gap; it needs a real drawable and the layout had to settle first.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:configure="com.cristianprincipi.habits.feature.widget.HabitWidgetConfigActivity"
    android:description="@string/widget_habit_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minHeight="80dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="80dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
